 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Then back channel is your friend. It' a light touch with your thumb that feels like a light brush of screen. It lasts for hours on battery life. Yes, it's very quiet. Some people also switch one hand mode and use your right hand thumb for back channel. Some laptops come with good built in back channel, so it' worth checking your settings first. If it still bugs you, then thin wedge can make a big difference. Then there are stick on pads that stick to the back of the keyboard. Try using your pinky as a trigger finger for small keystrokes like space and the one right next to the track pad. It gives your ring finger a rest and saves you from tangling.",
